  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31197472",
      "title": "Configuring the TextInput Field",
      "lectureOrder": 51,
      "videoOrder": 48,
      "sourceHash": "70f822d7a63823ec74e215d0fe768fdfa6801fbedcff8935a37331b6726dfdcc",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.02,
          "end": 3.93,
          "en": "So let's now dig a bit deeper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.93,
          "end": 5.61,
          "en": "into this text input field",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.61,
          "end": 7.83,
          "en": "and learn how we can configure it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.83,
          "end": 11.12,
          "en": "We already set a max length, but I also, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.12,
          "end": 15.1,
          "en": "wanna control which kind of characters can be entered there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.1,
          "end": 19.21,
          "en": "or to be precise, I wanna control which keyboard I get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.21,
          "end": 22.453,
          "en": "when I get a keyboard on my mobile device.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.49,
          "end": 24.94,
          "en": "Because at the moment, as I show you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.94,
          "end": 26.45,
          "en": "we get the regular keyboard",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.45,
          "end": 28.29,
          "en": "with all those regular characters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.29,
          "end": 30.56,
          "en": "and that's not what I want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.56,
          "end": 34.47,
          "en": "Now, text input allows you to control which keyboard",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.47,
          "end": 36.62,
          "en": "is opened by the device.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.62,
          "end": 41.62,
          "en": "And it can be controlled with the keyboard type prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.99,
          "end": 46.88,
          "en": "Now, this keyboard type prop takes a bunch of values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.88,
          "end": 49.6,
          "en": "And it's worth a look at the official docs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.6,
          "end": 53.72,
          "en": "to understand which values are supported on which platform.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.72,
          "end": 57.34,
          "en": "If you take a look at the keyboard type prop description",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.34,
          "end": 60.37,
          "en": "in the official docs for the text input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.37,
          "end": 62.92,
          "en": "you'll learn that there are a couple of values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.92,
          "end": 65.71,
          "en": "that work across platforms.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.71,
          "end": 68.58,
          "en": "And then there are values which are only available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.58,
          "end": 70.47,
          "en": "on one of the platforms.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.47,
          "end": 74.03999999999999,
          "en": "So for example, URL is supported on iOS devices,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.03999999999999,
          "end": 75.283,
          "en": "but not on Android.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.23,
          "end": 79.33,
          "en": "Now here, I wanna use the number-pad though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.33,
          "end": 81.81,
          "en": "which works across platforms,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.81,
          "end": 83.87,
          "en": "because this will open up a keyboard",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.87,
          "end": 87.07300000000001,
          "en": "that only shows numbers, which is is what I want here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 88.06,
          "end": 92.543,
          "en": "So therefore here all set keyboard type two number pad.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.82,
          "end": 97.52000000000001,
          "en": "Now, there also are a couple of other properties we can set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.52000000000001,
          "end": 100.74000000000001,
          "en": "And you see that there are a lot of props that are supported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 100.74000000000001,
          "end": 103.34,
          "en": "and definitely feel free to browse through them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.34,
          "end": 105.39,
          "en": "to understand which options you have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 105.39,
          "end": 107.333,
          "en": "when working with text inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.5,
          "end": 110.53999999999999,
          "en": "Here I, for example, also wanna set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 110.53999999999999,
          "end": 113.91,
          "en": "the auto capitalized option to none.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.91,
          "end": 116.71000000000001,
          "en": "It's not too important when working with numbers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.71000000000001,
          "end": 119.15,
          "en": "but if this would contain regular text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 119.15,
          "end": 122.1,
          "en": "this would ensure that it's not auto capitalized.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 122.1,
          "end": 124.25,
          "en": "Again, that's not really important here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 124.25,
          "end": 127.63,
          "en": "but I wanna show that this kind of prop exists.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 127.63,
          "end": 130.35,
          "en": "We also have a auto correct prop that allows us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 130.35,
          "end": 133.35,
          "en": "to turn auto correction on or off.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 133.35,
          "end": 135.87,
          "en": "Because it could, for example, be super annoying",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 135.87,
          "end": 139.67000000000002,
          "en": "if you have a field where users should enter their email,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 139.67000000000002,
          "end": 142.07,
          "en": "and you have auto capitalization",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 142.07,
          "end": 144.6,
          "en": "and auto correction turned on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 144.6,
          "end": 148.26,
          "en": "We all know these input fields where your email address",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 148.26,
          "end": 151.97,
          "en": "gets corrected and the first character gets capitalized,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 151.97,
          "end": 153.95,
          "en": "and you have to fix it thereafter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 153.95,
          "end": 156.84,
          "en": "You can avoid such bad user experiences",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 156.84,
          "end": 158.74,
          "en": "with props like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 158.74,
          "end": 162.11,
          "en": "Again, for this input where we only expect numbers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 162.11,
          "end": 163.753,
          "en": "this is not really needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 164.61,
          "end": 168.57,
          "en": "Now with that, if we save everything and I go back,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 168.57,
          "end": 171.34,
          "en": "you see immediately that on Android,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 171.34,
          "end": 175.27,
          "en": "we now get a different keyboard which only shows us numbers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 175.27,
          "end": 177.293,
          "en": "And it's the same here on iOS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 178.26,
          "end": 180.32,
          "en": "And that is a huge step forward,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 180.32,
          "end": 184.05,
          "en": "because that is the behavior we want for this input field.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 184.05,
          "end": 186.343,
          "en": "And that's of course pretty nice to have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 187.33,
          "end": 190.8,
          "en": "Therefore as a next step, let's leave this input field",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 190.8,
          "end": 193.93,
          "en": "and let's work on these buttons before we then start working",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 193.93,
          "end": 197.22,
          "en": "on the layout of this box by making sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 197.22,
          "end": 199.963,
          "en": "that these elements are laid out of bit nicer.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
